        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{\\log_{3}\\left(x^{2}\\right)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{3}\\left(x^{2}\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\,\\Longrightarrow\\,\\frac{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\log_{3}\\left(x^{2}\\right)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =1\\int \\log_{3}\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =1\\int u\\cdot \\frac{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{u^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} (\\log_{3}\\left(x^{2}\\right))^{2}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
